abstract: >-
  Guará is a runtime-assurance (RTA) boundary aligned with the ASTM F3269 architecture that
  bounds an untrusted complex function — a classical planner, a neural policy or a language
  model — around two flight platforms: PX4 aircraft through ROS 2 (implemented and measured
  in SITL) and F´ spacecraft flight software (specified). Monitors generated from FRETish
  requirements with NASA's FRET, Ogma and Copilot, a geofence predictor and a DAIDALUS
  detect-and-avoid node feed a fixed-period switching core that hands the vehicle to the
  platform's own recovery function inside a measured end-to-end latency. Every quantitative
  claim is reproduced from a recorded run.
